  "methodological_caveats": [
    "One-step K1 check uses local field r=H(sa)/(sa) at a selected symmetry-orbit representative; threshold T=0 was an exploratory fixed choice, not pre-registered.",
    "Input amplitude/sign guide at 20sites is a precomputed exact-reference lookup callable; not a scalable or learned NQS.",
    "Proposals use pre-trained same-chamber AVSL08 9-feature geometry-only policy with 400 prior single-orbit energy-label training checks; 160 attempts per arm are not training-cost-equivalent.",
    "First-state FN walker roots reused from genuine mixed FN branching simulation; no direct FN sampler restart in first stage.",
    "Finite list of exception-orbit sign flips is globally callable only because symmetry enumeration is affordable at 20 sites.",
    "Second-stage uses exact phi_FN for guide refresh; this creates a separate guide-only energy improvement ~5.6e-3 that MUST NOT be attributed to the second sign change.",
    "Three second-step cases do not show robust transfer or amortization; no 6x6 result, and no region-component C_w implemented."
  ],
